1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,058
Never sell what follows you.

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:08,800
Long ago, a fisherman on this island caught nothing for forty days.

3
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:13,900
On the forty-first night, a woman made of mist rose from the sea.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,100
“Give me your shadow,” she whispered, “and your nets will never be empty.”

5
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,470
What use is a shadow? He agreed.

6
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,500
From that dawn, his nets overflowed.

7
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:31,300
But at noon, the village whispered: “That man casts no shadow.”

8
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:34,271
His own wife would not look at him.

9
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:37,300
So he rowed out, to beg for it back.

10
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:41,000
She gave it back. But it would not follow him.

11
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:44,526
It walked into the sea. And he followed it.

12
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:49,200
On still nights, two shadows cross the bay.

13
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:52,386
Neither of them belongs to a man.
